<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Electronics on Brainbox Embedded Notes</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/site.notes2/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/</link><description>Recent content in Electronics on Brainbox Embedded Notes</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://brainboxemb.github.io/site.notes2/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>HUB75 Power Connections</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/site.notes2/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-connections/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/site.notes2/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-connections/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A prototype concept for distributing 5 V power from one supply to the HUB75 LED matrix panels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="proposed-concept"&gt;Proposed concept&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/site.notes2/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-connections/power-distribution-concept.svg" alt="HUB75 power distribution prototype concept"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The prototype is deliberately simple:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1 × removable 20 A input&lt;/strong&gt; for the main 5 V supply;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 × 4-pole barrier-strip terminals&lt;/strong&gt; for the HUB75 panel outputs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1 × additional 2-pole 10 A screw terminal&lt;/strong&gt; for PCB / auxiliary 5 V;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;all mounted on a &lt;strong&gt;4 × 6 cm double-sided experiment PCB&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The two 4-pole barrier strips provide eight screw positions in total. Five positions are intended for the five HUB75 panel feeds, leaving three spare positions.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Power Distribution Examples</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/site.notes2/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-distribution-examples/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/site.notes2/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-distribution-examples/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Examples that inspired the HUB75 power-distribution concept.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These are &lt;strong&gt;references, not the proposed design&lt;/strong&gt;. Images are deliberately shown as small thumbnails (maximum 300 px wide). Clicking an image or product name opens the original product page.&lt;/p&gt;
